import{_ as i,o as t,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 346 | Perfect-Work Dark Beings Setting: Victims and Perpetrators of the Predatory System","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 346 | Perfect-Work Dark Beings Setting: Victims and Perpetrators of the Predatory System","no":346,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Perfect World","Dark Beings","Victims","Perpetrators","Dialectics"],"related":["57-Dark Replacement Body Origin and Essence","59-Four Sub-Branches of Dark Replacement Body Disposal","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0346_模块2-完美世界-掠夺体系的受害者与加害者.md","filePath":"en/0346_模块2-完美世界-掠夺体系的受害者与加害者.md"}'),r={name:"en/0346_模块2-完美世界-掠夺体系的受害者与加害者.md"};function s(o,e,l,d,h,c){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-346-perfect-work-dark-beings-setting-victims-and-perpetrators-of-the-predatory-system" tabindex="-1">Entry 346 | Perfect-Work Dark Beings Setting: Victims and Perpetrators of the Predatory System <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-346-perfect-work-dark-beings-setting-victims-and-perpetrators-of-the-predatory-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 346 | Perfect-Work Dark Beings Setting: Victims and Perpetrators of the Predatory System&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Perfect-Work Full Decomposition (Entry 23) | Benchmark base: Documents 57, 59, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-are-dark-beings-born-evil-or-forced-into-evil-by-the-system" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Are dark beings born evil, or forced into evil by the system? <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-are-dark-beings-born-evil-or-forced-into-evil-by-the-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Are dark beings born evil, or forced into evil by the system?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Perfect World&#39;s dark beings are often set as pure evil — devouring for a living, beyond redemption. But Heng Yuan Zhou, using the causal self-discipline axiom, asks: are they born this way, or did the predatory system force them into perpetrators? This entry takes the six top-level axioms as base — anti-predation axiom, republican axiom of Myriad Races, collective ascension axiom, causal self-discipline axiom, law-first axiom (core), universal equal infinite law — to view dark beings dialectically. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Protagonist uniqueness dependency verdict: <strong>Shi Hao = extreme-leaning-medium / single-log tendency</strong>.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Labeling dark beings &quot;pure evil&quot; wastes:</p><ul><li>Forfeits the chance to understand their generation mechanism</li><li>Every problem simplified to &quot;kill&quot;; root-cure solution absent</li><li>After killing, new dark beings keep being produced</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Pure-evil setting&#39;s regression:</p><ol><li>Does not ask where darkness comes from</li><li>Suppression replaces transformation</li><li>Darkness forever burns without end</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Shi Hao&#39;s expeditions against dark beings:</p><ul><li>He is the &quot;perpetrator&quot;-fighter, yet rarely asks why they became perpetrators</li><li>Simplifies complex causality into good and evil</li><li>This simplification justifies his expeditions, yet also makes the dark source never run dry</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dark Beings (Pure-Evil Kill)</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis (Identify and Transform)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Born evil, kill them</td><td>Dark Replacement Body, identify origin</td></tr><tr><td>Suppress instead of transform</td><td>Four sub-branches classified disposal</td></tr><tr><td>Do not ask generation</td><td>Causal self-discipline, cut the generation</td></tr><tr><td>Regenerate after killing</td><td>Alaya early intervention</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Heng Yuan Zhou Documents 57 and 59 subdivide the &quot;Dark Replacement Body&quot; into origin and four sub-branch disposals — not presupposing them as pure evil, but treating them as a systemic phenomenon to identify, intervene, and transform.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Replicate the dark-beings generation chain</li><li>Inject two cases — &quot;kill&quot; vs. &quot;transform&quot;</li><li>Count dark-relapse rate</li><li>Output &quot;Dark Beings Dialectics Report&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-low</strong>. Dark beings&#39; essence changes across the trilogy</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong></li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: extreme-leaning-medium / single-log tendency</strong></li></ul><p>Add one layer: the dialectic of dark beings is that they are both perpetrators and the predatory system&#39;s aftereffects. Treating aftereffects as a new virus to kill, you never finish. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s four-sub-branch disposal of Dark Replacement Bodies reflects a cooler ethics — not presupposing them as pure evil, first asking where they come from, then deciding transform, isolate, or purge.</p><p>One closing line: the most responsible attitude toward darkness is not hate, but understanding. Understand where it comes from, then know where to act — this treats the root far better than killing one more batch of samples.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: killing does not solve generation</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: defining the predated as evil is second predation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo world&#39;s enemies are mostly aristocratic families; dark beings are system-alienated victims, more complex in nature</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: dark beings also have evolution qualification, yet are stripped</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: only transformation mechanisms can support the multiverse</li></ul><p>Add one more layer: treating dark beings as pure evil equals forfeiting the question why they became this way. And every root-cure solution starts from this forfeited question. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s classified disposal of Dark Replacement Bodies precisely picks this question back up.</p><ul><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="supplementary-analysis-dialectics-of-victim-and-perpetrator" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Analysis: Dialectics of Victim and Perpetrator <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-analysis-dialectics-of-victim-and-perpetrator" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Analysis: Dialectics of Victim and Perpetrator&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dark beings are both victims and perpetrators of the predatory system; this dual identity is fully recorded in the Alaya Network&#39;s archives. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization does not make a simple good-evil dichotomy of dark beings, but through the anti-predation axiom institutionally eliminates the soil that produces dark beings. The law-first axiom ensures the degenerate path is reversible — the Alaya Network provides repair channels for predators willing to turn back. The universal equal infinite law means dark beings are not permanently excluded from evolution rights.</p><h2 id="supplementary-analysis-redemption-and-transformation" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Analysis: Redemption and Transformation <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-analysis-redemption-and-transformation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Analysis: Redemption and Transformation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dark beings&#39; dual identity in Heng Yuan Zhou leads to a key institutional design: redemption channels. The Alaya Network provides a complete repair path for predators willing to turn back — stop predatory behavior, accept mind-repair, re-connect to the network after passing the law-cognition exam. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization sets no permanent banishment order; the law-first axiom ensures causal self-discipline is self-repair, not external punishment. The universal equal infinite law means dark beings are not stripped of evolution rights either — they merely took a detour; once the detour ends they can still return.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dark beings are both perpetrators and victims. Heng Yuan Zhou does not advocate being soft on evil, but insists: without understanding where evil comes from, you can only kill one batch, and another batch emerges. True root-cure is to cut the predatory rules that force people into darkness.</p><p>In the final analysis, Perfect World · victims and perpetrators of the predatory system described in this document are no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./334_模块2-完美世界-掠夺体系的必然产物.html">Entry 334 · Dark-Turmoil Source</a> · <a href="./354_模块2-完美世界-杜绝黑暗动乱的制度设计.html">Entry 354 · Alaya Supervision Plan</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/57-黑暗置换体起源与本质.html">57-Dark Replacement Body Origin and Essence</a></li></ul>',36)])])}const m=i(r,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
